# Nest is not the system of record

`server/` is the legacy TREK Nest + SQLite stack. Family domain data lives in Supabase (same project as iOS). Do not add family-domain endpoints, dual-write to SQLite, or treat Nest as a long-term BFF.

If you must touch Nest (bugfix, `VITE_DATA_PLANE=nest` compatibility):

- Match existing modules. Do not invent packages or import paths (`@nestjs/core/decorators`, TypeORM, `@nestjs/bull`, BullMQ).
- This server uses better-sqlite3, not TypeORM. Do not introduce TypeORM or `synchronize: true`.
- Return values through Nest handlers; do not bypass interceptors with raw `res.json` unless streaming.
- Server secrets stay in `server/.env*` — never `VITE_*`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — new family SoR on Nest
@Post('trips')
createFamilyTrip(@Body() dto: CreateTripDto) { return this.sqlite.insert(dto) }

// ✅ GOOD — leave domain writes to client Supabase adapters / RPCs
```

Do not rewrite Nest numeric TREK ids to UUID as a drive-by. UUID-first applies to supabase-plane adapters, not a Nest schema migration.
